## Layout

- `main.bot` — the workflow: one adaptive `campaign` agent carrying the
  mission (its system prompt is the `mission` prompt block).
- `manifest.yaml` — catalog metadata (name, icon, when_to_use, triggers).
- `skills/` — drop `SKILL.md` files here to ship knowledge with the bot;
  they are mirrored into the run workspace's `.claude/skills/`.
- `prompts/` — reusable `.md` prompts. The filename stem becomes the
  prompt name (`prompts/helper.md` → `system: helper`).
- `attachments/` — default binary inputs, referenced from
  `manifest.yaml`'s `attachments:` map.
- `presets/` — named launch-time biases (sous-bots). See
  `presets/example.md`.

## Run

```sh
iterion run {{.Slug}}/main.bot
iterion run {{.Slug}}/main.bot --preset example
```

Or from the studio: open the bot's page and hit Launch (or Test for a
throwaway run).

## Package

```sh
iterion bundle pack {{.Slug}}
```

Produces a deterministic `{{.Slug}}.botz` (same content → same bytes),
runnable with `iterion run {{.Slug}}.botz` and installable elsewhere.

See [docs/bundles.md](https://github.com/SocialGouv/iterion/blob/main/docs/bundles.md)
for the full format reference.
